class:: PitchRegisterOsc
summary:: Sample-coherent pitch register driving an oscillator family
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

PitchRegisterOsc is a language-side graph constructor. A small internal server
primitive shifts literal initial scale degrees on each audio-rate rising edge;
the language graph then uses DegreeToKey, Lag, and one oscillator per register
position. HarmonicStrideOsc supplies the preferred voices and Blip is the
dependency-free fallback.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/DegreeToKey::. DegreeToKey performs
the scale lookup, while PitchRegisterOsc also retains an ordered history,
glides its resulting frequencies, and sonifies every position.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: trig
Audio- or control-rate trigger. Each nonpositive-to-positive edge shifts
exactly once.

argument:: degree
New scale degree written into position zero on a trigger.

argument:: scaleBuf
Buffer containing scale semitone offsets for DegreeToKey.

argument:: root
Frequency in hertz corresponding to zero semitones.

argument:: initialDegrees
One to 32 finite literal degrees. Its size fixes output count and register
storage at construction.

argument:: harmonics
Literal harmonic limit from code::1:: through code::16384::.

argument:: decay
Harmonic decay used by HarmonicStrideOsc when available.

argument:: glide
Frequency smoothing time in seconds. It does not alter register timing.

argument:: mul
Multiplier applied independently to every voice.

argument:: add
Offset added to every voice after multiplication.

returns::
One audio channel per register position, newest degree first.

method:: kr

PitchRegisterOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

The register is implemented as a minimal native component because a downstream
audio Buffer reader can otherwise observe block-final LocalBuf state after
multiple same-block demand writes. Pitch conversion and synthesis deliberately
remain ordinary language-side graph construction. Voice phase offsets are
fixed by register index.

examples::

code::
(
Routine({
    var scale = Buffer.loadCollection(
        s, Scale.minorPentatonic.degrees
    );
    s.sync;
    {
        var trig = Impulse.ar(2);
        var degree = Demand.ar(
            trig, 0, Dseq([0, 2, 4, 7, 5, 3], inf)
        );
        Splay.ar(
            PitchRegisterOsc.ar(trig, degree, scale, 55)
        ) * 0.045;
    }.play;
}).play;
)
::

code::
(
Routine({
    var scale = Buffer.loadCollection(s, Scale.dorian.degrees);
    s.sync;
    {
        var trig = Dust.ar(3);
        var degree = Demand.ar(trig, 0, Drand((0..14), inf));
        Splay.ar(
            PitchRegisterOsc.ar(
                trig, degree, scale, 46,
                initialDegrees: [0, -2, -4, -7],
                harmonics: 24, decay: 0.85, glide: 0.04
            )
        ) * 0.04;
    }.play;
}).play;
)
::

